title: mf_hash
tags: [[Reserved field]] [[File fingerprint]]
kind: reference
summary: Marks the files whose full hash is kept fresh; inherited down mfr_path, off by default.

`true` marks a file, or everything under a directory, as worth a full hash kept
current ([[Content hashes kept fresh]]); `false` opts a subtree out again. Like
`mf_watch` it is inherited down the `mfr_path` tree: the nearest ancestor that sets
it, the record itself included, wins, and a record with none is not marked. It is
written without `force` and synced like any `mf_*` field, so the two sides of a link
agree on it.

A marked file is hashed again in the background after each change the watcher sees;
reconcile's part and sync's use of the hash are still being built.
